From 9e726ee914af86e79048fec21ac51a2550cfc83a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 11:36:46 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(sim): judge the probe's stylus stem and body in the
 protected-move law

The Probe op swept only the stylus ball against the model, so a deep
edge or corner touch beside a taller wall, or under an overhang, passed
while the stem or the probe body met the part. The law now also runs
the verifier's solid law (verify::solid_hits) with the probe stack from
probe_op::stylus_cutter: ball as the cutting atom, the stem (ball radius,
up to the stylus length) and the probe body (plus any holder) as the
bands. A stem or body that meets the part on any move is a ShankHit on
the part, a rapid that meets it RapidInStock; both hold the post. The
expected contact excuses nothing above the ball. The ball law is
unchanged and a move it convicted is not reported twice.

Pinned by probe_reach.rs: a_stem_that_meets_an_overhang_is_a_shank_hit,
a_body_that_meets_a_tall_wall_is_a_shank_hit,
clean_touches_stay_clean_under_the_reach_law,
the_stylus_stack_is_ball_then_stem_then_body,
a_short_stylus_deep_on_the_stock_edge_is_refused_by_the_op.

Fixes #172

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
